# CORE_JS — platform

Shared primitives for all CORE apps. Details: `ai-instructions/services.md`, `ai-instructions/README.md`.

## Services (`$svc`)

- **`$svc('name')`** is the only service accessor after bootstrap — never bypass with ad-hoc singletons.
- Register in app `Core` subclass via `registerService(name, Class)` — see `Core.registerAllServices()` for the platform kernel list.
- **`window.$core`** holds the app Core instance; **`window.$svc`** resolves registered services.
- Do **not** call `super.registerAllServices()` in app Core — opt-in only the services the app needs.

## Logging

- No `console.log` — use `$svc('log')` when needed; never at script load time.

## Ajax (`Core_AjaxService`)

- Ajax is a generic transport primitive used by an owning service, not directly by components — see `core-js-io-boundaries.mdc`.
- **2xx HTTP:** observable emits body; functional statuses (`SUCCESS`, …) stay in payload — handle in app code.
- **Transport failure:** observable **errors** with `{ kind: 'transport', … }` — no `alert()` in CORE.
- Apps override `getDefaultHeaders()` for CSRF, client version, etc.

## ESM imports

- Relative imports between CORE_JS modules **must include `.js` extension**.

## Router (query on same pathname)

- Match routes on pathname only (`getRelativePath()`); query changes on the same route must not remount the component.
- Emit `routeChanged` once per recognized query-only navigation; optional `detail.search` is additive — `detail.url` stays the pathname match.

## DOM / subscriptions

- User/API strings: `textContent` / `createElement({ text })`. `trustedHtml` for author-controlled markup only.
- `addSub()` for persistent subscriptions (BehaviorSubject), not one-shot application operations.

## Before adding code here

Generic primitive, no app domain, no `<core-*>` UI → CORE_JS. Component lifecycle → `core-js-components.mdc`. See `ai-instructions/layering.md`.
